    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d459">

                <pb facs="0595" n="515" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg515"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Griscom.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-01-04"><hi rendition="#italic">January 4,
                        1901</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 329.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 295, of the 12th ultimo, reporting the courtesies shown by the
                    Sultan to Captain Chester and his staff, of the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kentucky</hi>, during the recent visit of that vessel to
                    Constantinople.</p>
                <p>You will express to His Majesty, through the proper channel, this Government’s
                    appreciation of the courtesies shown to Captain Chester and his officers.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
